- `decode(encode(model))` succeeds for every well-formed persistent model;
- the decoded model is persistently equivalent to the original model;
- persistent equivalence compares all saved weights, all saved configuration fields, dimensions, layer count, and serialized floating-point bit patterns;
- invalid magic, unsupported version, malformed rank, malformed dimensions, truncated byte stream, oversized dimensions, invalid Boolean encoding, invalid checksum, and forbidden trailing data produce the specified errors;
