Keep regression tests only as executable checks. Do not use them as evidence for universal correctness. Label them clearly as tests.

All core correctness properties must be stated as universally quantified Lean theorems with explicit assumptions and explicit postconditions. Tests using fixed values such as repeated `0.25` or `0.5` inputs must not appear inside the final formal correctness theorem.

