8. Backward propagation proves derivative or adjoint correctness, not only output dimensions.
9. Registry acquisition, release, destruction, active-operation accounting, and handle ownership are modeled as real state transitions and proven safe.
10. Serialization roundtrip preserves every persistent field and f32 bit pattern, while malformed files are rejected correctly.
11. GPU and concurrency are either fully modeled and proven or explicitly excluded from the verified scope.
12. A formal Zig-to-Lean refinement relation connects the verified Lean semantics to the actual Zig implementation inside the declared verification boundary.
13. No final theorem derives “verification” from preassigned `true` values, trivial `Eq.refl` branch classification, list length, or dimension equality alone.
